{"root_text": {"uid": "sn46.15", "lang": "en", "is_root": false, "title": "Ill (2)", "author": "Bhikkhu Bodhi", "author_short": "Bodhi", "author_uid": "bodhi", "next": {"author_uid": "bodhi", "lang": "en", "name": "Sick (3rd) ", "uid": "sn46.16"}, "previous": {"author_uid": "bodhi", "lang": "en", "name": "Sick (1st) ", "uid": "sn46.14"}, "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n<meta name='author' content='Bhikkhu Bodhi'>\n<title></title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<article id='sn46.15' lang='en'>\n<header>\n<ul>\n<li class='division' lang='pli' translate='no'>Saṁyutta Nikāya</li>\n<li>Connected Discourses on the Factors of Enlightenment</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>46.15. Ill (2)</h1>\n</header>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc1' href='#sc1'>SC 1</a>On one occasion the Blessed One was dwelling at Rajagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the Squirrel Sanctuary. Now on that occasion the Venerable Mahamoggallana was dwelling on Mount Vulture Peak—sick, afflicted, gravely ill. Then, in the evening, the Blessed One emerged from seclusion and approached the Venerable Mahamoggallana … <span class='add'>all as above, with the change of names being the only difference</span> … In such a way the Venerable Mahamoggallana was cured of his illness. <a class='ref pts-vp-pli' id='sn.v.81' href='#sn.v.81'>sn.v.81</a> </p>\n<footer>\n<p>© Bhikkhu Bodhi, <cite class='book' translate='no'>The Connected Discourses of the Buddha</cite> (Wisdom Publications, <span class='publication-date'>2000</span>)</p>\n<p>This excerpt from <cite class='book' translate='no'>The Connected Discourses of the Buddha</cite> by <a href='http://www.wisdompubs.org/author/bhikkhu-bodhi'><span class='author'>Bhikkhu Bodhi</span></a> is licensed under a <a href='http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/deed.en_US' rel='license'>Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivs 3.0 Unported License</a>.</p>\n<p>Based on the work <a href='http://www.wisdompubs.org/book/connected-discourses-buddha'><cite class='book' translate='no'>Connected Discourses of the Buddha</cite></a> at Wisdom Publications.</p>\n<p>Permissions beyond the scope of this license may be available at <a href='http://www.wisdompubs.org/terms-use'>Wisdom Publications</a>.</p>\n<p>Prepared for SuttaCentral by <span class='editor'>Blake Walsh</span>.</p>\n</footer>\n</article>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}, "translation": {"uid": "sn46.15", "lang": "en", "is_root": false, "title": "Ill (2)", "author": "Bhikkhu Bodhi", "author_short": "Bodhi", "author_uid": "bodhi", "next": {"author_uid": "bodhi", "lang": "en", "name": "Sick (3rd) ", "uid": "sn46.16"}, "previous": {"author_uid": "bodhi", "lang": "en", "name": "Sick (1st) ", "uid": "sn46.14"}, "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n<meta name='author' content='Bhikkhu Bodhi'>\n<title></title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<article id='sn46.15' lang='en'>\n<header>\n<ul>\n<li class='division' lang='pli' translate='no'>Saṁyutta Nikāya</li>\n<li>Connected Discourses on the Factors of Enlightenment</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>46.15. Ill (2)</h1>\n</header>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc1' href='#sc1'>SC 1</a>On one occasion the Blessed One was dwelling at Rajagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the Squirrel Sanctuary. Now on that occasion the Venerable Mahamoggallana was dwelling on Mount Vulture Peak—sick, afflicted, gravely ill. Then, in the evening, the Blessed One emerged from seclusion and approached the Venerable Mahamoggallana … <span class='add'>all as above, with the change of names being the only difference</span> … In such a way the Venerable Mahamoggallana was cured of his illness. <a class='ref pts-vp-pli' id='sn.v.81' href='#sn.v.81'>sn.v.81</a> </p>\n<footer>\n<p>© Bhikkhu Bodhi, <cite class='book' translate='no'>The Connected Discourses of the Buddha</cite> (Wisdom Publications, <span class='publication-date'>2000</span>)</p>\n<p>This excerpt from <cite class='book' translate='no'>The Connected Discourses of the Buddha</cite> by <a href='http://www.wisdompubs.org/author/bhikkhu-bodhi'><span class='author'>Bhikkhu Bodhi</span></a> is licensed under a <a href='http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/deed.en_US' rel='license'>Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivs 3.0 Unported License</a>.</p>\n<p>Based on the work <a href='http://www.wisdompubs.org/book/connected-discourses-buddha'><cite class='book' translate='no'>Connected Discourses of the Buddha</cite></a> at Wisdom Publications.</p>\n<p>Permissions beyond the scope of this license may be available at <a href='http://www.wisdompubs.org/terms-use'>Wisdom Publications</a>.</p>\n<p>Prepared for SuttaCentral by <span class='editor'>Blake Walsh</span>.</p>\n</footer>\n</article>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}, "segmented": false, "suttaplex": {"acronym": "SN 46.15", "alt_acronym": null, "volpages": "PTS SN 5.80", "alt_volpages": null, "uid": "sn46.15", "blurb": "When Mahāmoggallāna was sick, the Buddha recited to him the awakening factors, inspiring him to a swift recovery.", "difficulty": null, "original_title": "Dutiyagilānasutta", "root_lang": "pli", "root_lang_name": "Pāli", "type": "leaf", "from": null, "translated_title": "Sick (2nd) ", "translations": [{"lang": "de", "lang_name": "Deutsch", "is_root": false, "author": "Sabbamitta", "author_short": "sabbamitta", "author_uid": "sabbamitta", "publication_date": "2019", "id": "sn46.15_translation-de-sabbamitta", "segmented": true, "title": "Krank (2) ", "volpage": null, "has_comment": false}, {"lang": "en", "lang_name": "English", "is_root": false, "author": "Bhikkhu Sujato", "author_short": "sujato", "author_uid": "sujato", "publication_date": "2018", "id": "sn46.15_translation-en-sujato", "segmented": true, "title": "Sick (2nd) ", "volpage": null, "has_comment": false}, {"lang": "pli", "lang_name": "Pāli", "is_root": true, "author": "Mahāsaṅgīti Tipiṭaka Buddhavasse 2500", "author_short": "ms", "author_uid": "ms", "publication_date": null, "id": "sn46.15_root-pli-ms", "segmented": true, "title": null, "volpa